<title>CHILE: Rio Algom Chile copper output rises.</title>
<headline>Rio Algom Chile copper output rises.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copper production at Canadian mining company Rio Algom's Chilean Cerro Colorado mine rose to 59,324 tonnes of cathodes last year from 36,443 tonnes in 1995, said the pit's sales manager Verena Horst.</p>
<p>The company expects output to be close to the mine's 60,000 design capacity tonne this year, Horst told Reuters.</p>
<p>Rio Algom has started building work on an expansion at the pit which will increase its capacity to 100,000 tonnes in mid-1998, she said.</p>
<p>Horst said the expansion will cost $200 million.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
